      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Requested dose:** ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day.\n- **Maximum daily dose:** the usual maximum for adults in a monitored setting is 3,200 mg/day. Over-the-counter use is capped at 1,200 mg/day.\n- **Maximum single dose:** a single dose is usually capped at 800 mg, so 1600 mg per dose is double that.\n- **Risks at this dose:** GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't make this dose safe.\n\nThe order may be a typo or a total daily dose entered as a per-dose amount. Common regimens would be:\n\n- 400 mg PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n- 600 mg PO four times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you intend and I'll enter it. If you really do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that. I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
